21z8|n|An offensive weapon, having a long and usually sharp/pointed blade with a cutting edge or edges. It is the general term, including the small sword, rapier, saber, scimiter, and many other varieties. ; Hence, the emblem of judicial vengeance or punishment, or of authority and power. ; Destruction by the sword, or in battle; war; dissension. ; The military power of a country. ; One of the end bars by which the lay of a hand loom is suspended.	v:nl3,150,1~nl3,150,1	n:nl3,150,1~nl3,150,1
